WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.210
- The Gilbert U-238 Atomic Energy Lab.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:05.310
The Atomic Energy Lab was
designed to help children

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.790
learn how to make nuclear
weapons, seriously.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.210
Sometimes kids' toys can
have adult consequences.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.980
When you were a kid, did
you ever wish for a toy

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.964
that seemed a little too dangerous?

00:00:15.964 --> 00:00:18.111
- No, no, I want an official
Red Ryder carbine-action

00:00:18.111 --> 00:00:19.713
200 shot range model air rifle.

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:22.233
- You'll shoot your eye out kid.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.600
- From lawn darts to easy bake ovens

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:27.030
it seems that toy makers
secretly want to kill you.

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:29.010
They've invented toy
weapons, deadly dolls,

00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:31.950
and lab kits containing
asbestos and even uranium.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:33.270
So let's put on our lawyer hat

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:34.920
and look at some of
the most dangerous toys

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:36.480
that have ever been invented

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.930
and discuss how legal
or illegal they were.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:41.190
Now, there was a time when 'CSI'

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.620
was the most popular TV show in the world.

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.610
The show aired at 10:00 PM

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:45.900
and obviously was geared towards

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.490
and mostly popular with adults.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:50.100
But the thing is, why monetize just adults

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.309
when you can also monetize children?

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:56.035
(rockstar screams)

00:00:56.035 --> 00:00:57.870
So the executives at CBSs capitalized

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.100
on the popularity of 'CSI'

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.280
by giving Planet Toys a license
to make 'CSI' themed toys.

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.960
The company passed on the obvious choices,

00:01:03.960 --> 00:01:06.315
sunglasses for David Caruso wannabes.

00:01:06.315 --> 00:01:08.070
(rockstar screams)

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.960
And instead came up with
two fingerprint kits

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.050
for kids who shouldn't be
watching the show anyway.

00:01:13.050 --> 00:01:15.540
But this quickly turned
into a fiasco when tests

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:18.600
conducted by the Asbestos
Disease Awareness Organization

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.460
revealed that the kits
contained white powder

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:22.560
that consisted of 7% tremolite,

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:25.110
one of the most dangerous
forms of asbestos.

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:27.930
Asbestos is a potent
carcinogen in any form

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:29.610
but it poses the greatest health risk

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:31.590
when it is in tiny particulates

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.630
which are allowed to become airborne

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.460
and easily enter the body.

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:37.560
This is precisely the form that it took

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.300
in the 'CSI' forensics kit.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.530
When confronted with the test results,

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.730
Planet Toys told retailers

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.830
to stop sales of the 'CSI' exam kit.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:44.730
However, the company refused

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.410
to stop selling the 'CSI' lab kit

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.360
which contained the
same fingerprint powder

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.180
and it refused to voluntarily
recall either of the products.

00:01:51.180 --> 00:01:53.100
As you might have guessed,
this didn't end well

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.710
for Planet Toys, which filed
for Chapter seven bankruptcy

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:59.730
in 2009, declaring liabilities
of at least 10 million.

00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:01.560
Chapter seven bankruptcy
is the kind of bankruptcy

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.500
where there's no reorganization
or managing of debts.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.060
The company just gives up.

00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:07.590
A good idea to quit while you're ahead

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.060
instead of losing a bunch of money

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:12.420
in seeing the mesothelioma
consequences of your actions

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.710
40 years down the line.

00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.930
And not surprisingly, CBS later settled

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:16.830
a class action lawsuit

00:02:16.830 --> 00:02:19.350
brought by the people who
had purchased those kits.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.903
Now that takes us to the Swing Wing.

00:02:21.903 --> 00:02:24.797
♪ A brand new Transogram fun thing ♪

00:02:24.797 --> 00:02:26.408
- [Announcer] It's a what?

00:02:26.408 --> 00:02:28.110
♪ It's a Swing Wing ♪

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:29.310
- The Swing Wing was invented

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.750
by an out of work chiropractor.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.070
No, that's not a joke.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:33.750
Now, how do you think your neck would feel

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:35.520
after five minutes of this motion?

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:37.080
Look at this kid go.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:38.430
This toy consists of a ribbon

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:39.690
with weighted balls attached to it,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.280
which fits around a child's head,

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:42.780
kind like a cranial weed wacker.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:45.090
Now, I can't imagine what could go wrong

00:02:45.090 --> 00:02:48.300
with a rope that's being
swung around a child's neck.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.000
Look, elephants and monkeys
enjoy watching kids use it

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.610
which isn't an unorthodox
way to market a toy.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:58.170
Also, maybe those elephants
and monkeys are just hungry

00:02:58.170 --> 00:03:00.030
and waiting for kids to commit

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:02.070
their own sort of Darwin Award.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:03.720
Not surprisingly, the
Swing Wing was pulled

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.420
from shelves because many
kids who played with the toy

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.060
suffered cerebral hemorrhages
and neck injuries.

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:10.770
Who would've predicted
that whipping your head

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.510
back and forth with weighted balls

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:13.767
would be bad for you?

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:15.870
Now the bestselling toy for boys in 1964

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.574
was the Johnny Seven One Man Army.

00:03:18.574 --> 00:03:19.407
(rapid gunfire)

00:03:19.407 --> 00:03:21.630
- [Announcer] Your squad is ready

00:03:21.630 --> 00:03:23.790
for you to lead them through

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:26.670
with Johnny Seven, the One Man Army Gun.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.720
- Released during the Cold War,

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:29.040
this toy had everything kids needed

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.600
to survive their own Red Dawn

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.210
including a grenade
launcher, an anti-armor gun,

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:36.090
an anti-tank rocket,
an anti bunker missile,

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:39.300
a Tommy gun, and a semi-automatic
pistol that fired caps

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:41.220
with a rifle with 12 bullets.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.020
When fully deployed, this
toy was three feet long

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:43.980
and weighed four pounds.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.680
Four pounds of pure
military grade testosterone.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:48.600
Detective Goren demonstrated
all seven weapons

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.820
on an episode of Law and
Order criminal intent.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:52.500
- Seven weapons in one,

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.510
grenade launcher,
(gun pops)

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:56.760
anti-tank rocket,
(gun pops)

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:59.280
armor piercing shell,
(gun pops)

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.190
anti bunker missile,
(gun pops)

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:03.540
machine gun,
(gun clicks)

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.003
repeater rifle, cap gun.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:08.730
- I definitely want one.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:11.970
Also, I support military
interventionism now. That's weird.

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.070
But this toy is legendary.

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.690
Captain Kangaroo banned ads

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.850
for the Johnny Seven One Man Army

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:20.580
from his show because he didn't
want to promote violence.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.200
That of course just made it even cooler

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.930
and it's become a kind of
holy grail for toy collectors.

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:27.690
It can even be yours for
the low, low price of $450

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:29.910
on eBay with $60 for shipping.

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.380
Freedom ain't free baby.

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:34.110
So is it illegal to sell a toy like this?

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:35.460
Well, generally not.

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.840
1970s consumer advocates

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.090
petition the US Consumer
Product Safety Commission

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.430
to regulate or ban toy guns.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:42.990
The federal government
considered it for years

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.910
but eventually agreed to allow toy makers

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.190
to create their own list
of voluntary standards.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.020
These standards focus on warning labels

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.390
and clear instructions, but
leave the design of the toys

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.010
largely up to the manufacturer.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:56.040
Today there's just one federal
law regulating toy guns,

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.290
15 U.S.C. section 5001

00:04:58.290 --> 00:05:01.710
which requires toy guns to
have a blaze orange plug

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.440
on the muzzle to distinguish
toy guns from the real thing.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:07.380
This law was passed in 1986
and it applies retroactively

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:10.740
to all toys manufactured,
designed, and produced since 1898.

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.630
However, the law does
not stop the end user

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:14.070
from modifying the weapon.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:16.260
So today, the Johnny Seven
One Man Army would be illegal

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:17.850
unless they painted the muzzle orange.

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.110
But don't come crying to me

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.570
if the police shoot your
children as a result.

00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:22.403
I'm just kidding.

00:05:22.403 --> 00:05:24.177
The police will shoot
your children anyway.

00:05:24.177 --> 00:05:26.820
And now that takes us
from guns to vegetables.

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.610
Developed in 1978 by Xavier Roberts,

00:05:29.610 --> 00:05:32.820
Cabbage Patch Kids dolls were
all the rage in the 1980s

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:34.560
and came in many variations.

00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.030
Hasbro bought the rights to the brand

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.950
and started producing a
line of Cabbage Patch Kids

00:05:37.950 --> 00:05:39.240
with various functions.

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:43.140
Enter 1995 Snack Time Kids,
a munching and chewing doll,

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:44.970
which sounds like a nightmare.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:47.160
And for hundreds or thousands of kids

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.500
it probably did inspire a few nightmares.

00:05:49.500 --> 00:05:51.810
As you can see, the
dolls had moving mouths

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:55.680
and let kids feed these fat
dolls with plastic snacks.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.940
After the kids fed the doll,

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.980
the food was deposited into a backpack.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:01.650
Obviously this has all the
hallmarks of a bad idea.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:04.620
What kid would stop with the
plastic french fries and gum?

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:06.630
And why not try feeding
the doll's real food?

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:09.600
If parents weren't paying
attention and any food got stuck

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:11.490
the food just stayed
there until it rotted.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:13.380
But that wasn't the biggest
problem with these dolls.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.370
The biggest problem was

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:16.440
that these Snack Time Cabbage Patch kids

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.895
had a taste for human
flesh or at least hair.

00:06:19.895 --> 00:06:22.920
(terrified scream)
(booming thunder)

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.600
And the bigger problem was
that the doll didn't have

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:26.160
an on or an off switch.

00:06:26.160 --> 00:06:29.130
The mouth operated by
having rollers move the food

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:32.610
and if the food kept on coming,
the rollers kept on moving.

00:06:32.610 --> 00:06:34.320
This meant that kids got their hair caught

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.320
in a doll's mouth, which
was designed to keep rolling

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:39.930
up until whatever it bit
ended up in the backpack.

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:42.870
For some kids, that meant being
trapped for up to 30 minutes

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.400
while their parents dismantled the doll

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:45.720
by chopping it's head off

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:48.750
and then searching the body
cavity for the batteries.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:50.520
Hundreds of irate parents complained

00:06:50.520 --> 00:06:52.080
and Mattel voluntarily recalled the toys

00:06:52.080 --> 00:06:55.800
and paid $40 refunds to 500,000 people

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:58.350
who purchased this cannibal
Cabbage Patch Doll.

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.330
That takes us to Sky Dancers.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:02.460
Sky Dancers look innocent enough.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:04.023
These are dolls that can fly.

00:07:05.359 --> 00:07:06.340
- They're flying!

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.321
♪ Fly for me, just for me,
Sky Dancer dance for me ♪

00:07:10.321 --> 00:07:12.330
- Wow! They really fly!

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.940
- Just pull the string and watch
them soar like helicopters.

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:16.470
Children loved them and
they were popular enough

00:07:16.470 --> 00:07:18.510
to stay on the market from 1994

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:19.800
until the turn of the century

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.290
when the US government
declared them too dangerous.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:24.270
The US Consumer Product
Safety Commission is charged

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.190
with protecting the public
from unreasonable risks

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.740
of injury or death associated
with the use of thousands

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.210
of types of consumer products.

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:31.830
And according to the CPSC,

00:07:31.830 --> 00:07:33.840
Sky Dancers had a propensity to fly

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:36.210
and go in unpredictable directions

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.860
and causing all kinds of harm.

00:07:37.860 --> 00:07:38.940
And in fact, when I was a kid,

00:07:38.940 --> 00:07:41.250
I busted open my lip
with a similar product.

00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:43.140
Why? Because when you pull the string

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:46.110
you naturally put your
face directly in front

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.030
of the spinning death helicopters

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.800
and the hard plastic that was used

00:07:49.800 --> 00:07:52.200
for the wings could do some real damage.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.540
And the toy company received 170 reports

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.220
that the dolls were striking children

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.980
and adults resulting in
150 reports of injuries.

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.750
Injuries reported included eye injuries

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.830
including scratch corneas

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:03.660
and incidents of temporary blindness,

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:06.510
broken teeth, mild
concussion, a broken rib,

00:08:06.510 --> 00:08:08.820
and facial lacerations
that required stitches.

00:08:08.820 --> 00:08:11.340
But all's well that ends well
when the CPSC ordered a recall

00:08:11.340 --> 00:08:14.310
of 8.9 million Sky Dancers.

00:08:14.310 --> 00:08:16.110
Now, one of the best
ways to aggravate parents

00:08:16.110 --> 00:08:18.990
is to sell a toy that is
both noisy and dangerous.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.570
And that's just what toy
makers achieved with Klackers

00:08:21.570 --> 00:08:23.460
a kid version of bolas

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.550
a weapon that Argentinian
gauchos used to hunt.

00:08:26.550 --> 00:08:28.020
- [Announcer] The new
original miracle Klackers

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.090
won't shatter even if you use both hands.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:33.570
Try stereo klacking with
unbreakable miracle Klackers

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.300
- Bolas are a throwing weapon
made of weights on the end

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:37.830
of interconnected cords.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.090
In fact, the only real difference

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:40.680
between Klackers and the deadly bolas

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.890
is that Klackers are shorter
and not made of wood.

00:08:43.890 --> 00:08:45.750
Just like attorney Tom.

00:08:45.750 --> 00:08:47.250
Someday you'll be a real boy.

00:08:47.250 --> 00:08:49.320
Now rather than throwing them at animals

00:08:49.320 --> 00:08:50.640
to tangle up their legs,

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:52.350
kids were supposed to swing the Klackers

00:08:52.350 --> 00:08:54.337
until they made an ear splitting noise.

00:08:54.337 --> 00:08:56.100
(rockstar screaming)

00:08:56.100 --> 00:08:57.630
What could possibly go wrong?

00:08:57.630 --> 00:08:59.640
Well, they violate Legal
Eagle's rule number one

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.570
for kids' toys,

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:02.490
anything that can be used as a weapon

00:09:02.490 --> 00:09:04.650
will be used as a weapon.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:06.780
Now, the first Klackers
appeared in the late 60s

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:08.280
and they were made from tempered glass

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:11.190
which contrary to the marketing
about being unbreakable

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:12.540
would eventually shatter,

00:09:12.540 --> 00:09:15.090
pelting users with shards of glass.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:16.830
Eventually, the US government
classified Klackers

00:09:16.830 --> 00:09:19.110
as a mechanical hazard in the court case

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.600
and worst epic rap battle of history,

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:23.520
United States versus article consisting

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:26.160
of 50,000 cardboard boxes, more or less,

00:09:26.160 --> 00:09:28.440
each containing one pair of Klacker balls.

00:09:28.440 --> 00:09:29.700
Now this case became famous

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:31.050
because people were amused by the fact

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:33.240
that the government seemed to
have sued the Klacker balls

00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:36.060
and the boxes that they were
contained in themselves.

00:09:36.060 --> 00:09:36.930
But that's because the seizure

00:09:36.930 --> 00:09:39.180
was an exercise of jurisdiction in-rem.

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.500
Jurisdiction in-rem is a legal term

00:09:40.500 --> 00:09:43.380
describing the power a court
may exercise over property.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:45.360
It assumes that the property or status

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.790
is the primary object of the action.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:49.590
Classic cases involving
jurisdiction in-rem

00:09:49.590 --> 00:09:51.150
include United States versus

00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:53.910
one Tyrannosaurus Bataar skeleton,

00:09:53.910 --> 00:09:56.790
South Dakota versus 15 impounded cats,

00:09:56.790 --> 00:10:00.480
and one 1958 Plymouth
Sedan versus Pennsylvania.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.370
In the case of the Klackers,
the United States Marshals

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:04.260
seized a shipment of Klacker balls

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.810
and the Ace Novelty
Company filed a complaint

00:10:06.810 --> 00:10:08.400
against forfeiture
arguing that the shipment

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.230
was not a banned hazard

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:13.080
as defined by the Federal
Hazardous Substances Act.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.180
The government argued that
the Klackers were hazardous

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:19.230
as the term was defined in 16 CFR 1500.18

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.930
which bans toys presenting
a mechanical hazard.

00:10:21.930 --> 00:10:23.790
And while the Ace Novelty Company argued

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.320
that there was an exception,

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.420
the court sided with the US government

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.340
and eventually banned the bolas.

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:30.693
I mean children's toy.

00:10:30.693 --> 00:10:33.300
- [Announcer] Look for this package.

00:10:33.300 --> 00:10:34.560
- Now, just about everyone is familiar

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.650
with the Slip N' Slide
a staple of the summer.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:40.170
- [Announcer] Okay,
everybody come outside.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:42.846
Everybody ready for a wild wet ride?

00:10:42.846 --> 00:10:45.570
♪ Slip, Slip N' Slide. ♪

00:10:45.570 --> 00:10:47.700
The Slip N' Slide was
invented by Robert Carrier

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:49.380
after watching his son deliberately slide

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:52.140
across wet concrete and
carpet in the garage.

00:10:52.140 --> 00:10:53.850
Carrier was an upholster who worked

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:55.620
with a company that produced boat seats.

00:10:55.620 --> 00:10:58.290
So he borrowed a 50
foot roll of Naugahyde,

00:10:58.290 --> 00:10:59.190
installed a hose,

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.440
and invented one of the
most iconic summer toys.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:03.360
Carrier took his invention
to the Wham-O company,

00:11:03.360 --> 00:11:05.550
which was behind the popular
toys like the Frisbee

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:06.660
and the Hula Hoop.

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:08.460
Naugahyde was replaced with plastic

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.860
and the toy went on sale in 1961.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:12.270
Now obviously everyone loved it

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.300
and initially there were
few injuries reported

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:17.430
but the Slip N' Slide soon
encountered a problem.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.710
Kids loved it so much that
adults wanted to join in.

00:11:19.710 --> 00:11:23.325
Adults who maybe had a few too
many cans of lawsuit juice.

00:11:23.325 --> 00:11:24.158
(elevator music)

00:11:24.158 --> 00:11:27.150
Lawsuit juice. It's not beer, we swear.

00:11:27.150 --> 00:11:29.040
Okay, it's totally just beer.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.680
But the Slip N' Slide was
not designed for adults.

00:11:31.680 --> 00:11:33.270
The instruction said that
the product was designed

00:11:33.270 --> 00:11:34.530
for children 10 and over

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:37.290
and presumably that didn't
include youthful grownups.

00:11:37.290 --> 00:11:41.370
In 1987 a 34 year old man broke
his neck and was paralyzed

00:11:41.370 --> 00:11:42.600
after using a Slip N' Slide.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.970
A jury decided that the
Slip N' Slide was defective

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:46.140
and unreasonably dangerous

00:11:46.140 --> 00:11:48.540
and gave the plaintiff over $12 million.

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:51.060
In 1988, a University of
Central Florida student

00:11:51.060 --> 00:11:52.770
also broke his neck on the slide.

00:11:52.770 --> 00:11:53.970
He won his lawsuit as well

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:56.730
and the toy company took the
Slip N' Slide off the market.

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.930
Eventually, in 1993,

00:11:57.930 --> 00:11:59.640
the US Consumer Product Safety Commission

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:00.780
issued a recall notice

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:03.360
and the Slip N' Slide was Slip N' Shelved.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.770
Fortunately for kids, the Slip N' Slide

00:12:04.770 --> 00:12:06.240
has been given a new life.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:08.640
You can buy a new one
complete with a warning

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.740
that it's only safe for kids 12 and over.

00:12:10.740 --> 00:12:13.260
So to all of you kids and adults out there

00:12:13.260 --> 00:12:16.260
please Slip N' Slide responsibly.

00:12:16.260 --> 00:12:18.420
Or don't, I'm not your parent,

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.920
though I can represent you

00:12:19.920 --> 00:12:22.340
in a lawsuit over a horrific injury.

00:12:22.340 --> 00:12:26.257
(better Call Saul theme music)

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:29.790
Now, if these toys aren't
scary enough for you

00:12:29.790 --> 00:12:30.990
then you might be interested

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:34.320
in the Gilbert U-238 Atomic Energy Lab.

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:36.540
This set was created by
Alfred Carlton Gilbert

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:38.790
who was also the inventor
of the Erector Set.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.130
His Atomic Energy Lab was
designed to help children

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.170
learn how to make nuclear weapons.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:47.550
No, seriously. This toy actually
included uranium samples.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:48.900
It came with four glass jars

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.660
containing natural uranium
barium ore samples.

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.490
The goal was for kids
to learn how to create

00:12:53.490 --> 00:12:55.560
and watch nuclear and chemical reactions

00:12:55.560 --> 00:12:57.780
using radioactive materials.

00:12:57.780 --> 00:12:59.760
Obviously. How else are you gonna do it?

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:01.920
Gilbert insisted this was a safe toy

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:03.540
as long as you didn't break the seals

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:05.010
on the uranium samples.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:07.710
You know, how kids don't break
the toys that they're given.

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:09.930
Luckily, the lab included
a real Geiger counter,

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:12.120
an electroscope, a Wilson cloud chamber,

00:13:12.120 --> 00:13:14.130
and some low level radiation sources,

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:17.010
including zinc, polonium,
and ruthenium isotopes

00:13:17.010 --> 00:13:19.050
labeled alpha, beta,
and gamma, depending on

00:13:19.050 --> 00:13:21.150
which particular radiation
particles they emitted.

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.470
Now, the product catalog explains

00:13:22.470 --> 00:13:24.660
that the atomic reactions
are beautiful to watch.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:25.920
They're particularly beautiful

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:28.980
once you've had the kit long
enough to grow a third eyeball.

00:13:28.980 --> 00:13:31.230
And despite the hype,
this toy never caught on

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:33.690
and fewer than 5,000 kits were ever sold.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:35.850
It cost $47 in the 1950s

00:13:35.850 --> 00:13:38.850
which was the equivalent
of at least $550 today.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.520
Now, the Atomic Energy Lab
was meant to make kids smarter

00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:44.130
but it would've only resulted
in kids getting a third arm.

